-- allium: 3

-- Module: safe_to_evict.
-- Scope: when knarr sets cluster-autoscaler.kubernetes.io/safe-to-evict to
-- "false", when it removes it, and that it never writes "true" by default: the
-- threshold and its hysteresis against Cluster Autoscaler's blackout, pods
-- with local storage, caps that avoid pinning nodes, and the best-effort limits
-- (§6, §9.9). Grounded in Decision 0008 (spike S2a, ticket 15); GKE
-- confirmation is spike S2b (ticket 16).
-- Owner: ticket 25.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "§9.9 Threshold: the cost_mapping tier or tiers at or above which knarr writes \"false\", and its own hysteresis, wider than cost_mapping's margin (Decision 0008)."
open question "§9.9 Removal: that ending protection removes the annotation rather than writing \"true\", and what is written for pods with emptyDir or hostPath volumes (Decision 0008, Exp4)."
open question "§9.9 Pinning: the cap on the share of a workload's pods marked at once and on how long one mark is held, with expiry left to §9.12."
open question "§9.9 Best effort: how the clauses state that a mark is honoured only up to CA's one re-check and not once eviction has started (Decision 0008)."
open question "§9.9 GKE: which clauses spike S2b (ticket 16) must confirm on GKE's managed Cluster Autoscaler, including local-storage pods on control plane 1.22 or later."
